Hi Jungmin,

The server portion of mirtCAT is a private portion of the package, and is therefore difficult to edit directly. Exposing the server portion would require a good degree of modularization, which is on my radar to do as the current server.R file is rather convoluted and difficult for front-end users to parse (let alone edit). Your best bet at this point would unfortunately be to make a clone of the package, edit the server.R file directly from the package source, and build the customized version of the package. Not the most direct route, but in case you're still interested that would be the current solution. HTH.

Phil

